# Minco application agent instructions

This is a generated Minco application in application mode, not the Minco framework repository. Use
`$minco-web-application` for the end-to-end application workflow. Inspect
bounded project facts with `cargo minco agent context --json` or select one
operation with `cargo minco agent context --operation <operationId> --json`.

Set up repository-scoped Codex and Claude skills explicitly: first run
`cargo minco agent plan --target all --json`, review every action and conflict,
then run `cargo minco agent sync --target all --expect-plan-digest <sha256>` only
with approval for those exact writes. Never replace user-owned instructions.

1. `openapi/openapi.yaml` is the HTTP source of truth.
2. Never edit `crates/api/src/generated.rs` manually; run `cargo minco contract sync`.
3. Domain code must not depend on Axum, SQLx, AWS, Lambda, or generated contract DTOs.
4. Application code owns use cases and infrastructure-facing ports.
5. HTTP handlers map contract DTOs to exactly one application use case and contain no SQL.
6. Infrastructure implementations belong in `crates/adapters`.
7. Add a failing application or HTTP test before implementing business behavior.
8. Run `cargo minco check --with-cargo` before completing application work.
9. Deployment cost, wake-source, performance, and database-profile changes require explicit review.
10. Keep migration identity, ownership, risk, verification, and history in the
    selected root's `.minco-migrations.toml`; never change applied SQL only to
    change metadata.
11. Use `cargo minco db plan`, digest-bound `db migrate`, and `db verify`.
    Application startup must not migrate.
